s nearly $6.8 million on hand, dwarfing Smith's roughly $121,000 raised, with no meaningful outside spending on either side.\n\nEvery major race rater labels the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets give Merkley win probabilities between 93 and 98 percent. No general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on the state's partisan lean, incumbency, and the stark financial gap. The race is not competitive on current evidence, and attention is better spent on genuinely contested states.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9939, "margin": 17.74}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9912, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9925, "margin": 17.5}]}